1
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:07,462
This is Cover Studio, built for OkurmenKids:

2
00:00:07,482 --> 00:00:11,595
a modern platform for designing
document covers, certificates,

3
00:00:11,615 --> 00:00:13,261
reports and title slides.

4
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:18,180
Everything runs in the browser. You
pick a template, fill in your details,

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:21,661
fine-tune the design, and
download a print-ready A4 file.

6
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:25,313
In the next few minutes, we'll
walk through the real application,

7
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,914
and then look at how it's built.

8
00:00:30,934 --> 00:00:35,497
Schools, universities and training
centers produce a lot of documents:

9
00:00:35,517 --> 00:00:39,752
coursework title pages, project
covers, certificates and reports.

10
00:00:40,172 --> 00:00:43,347
Making each one by hand in
a graphics editor is slow,

11
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:45,638
and the results are rarely consistent.

12
00:00:46,059 --> 00:00:50,974
Cover Studio solves this with parametric
templates. You enter the content once —

13
00:00:50,994 --> 00:00:54,614
the topic, the author, the
supervisor and the institution —

14
00:00:54,634 --> 00:00:56,773
and the layout is composed for you.

15
00:00:57,197 --> 00:01:01,396
The interface itself is in Russian,
and some templates are in Kyrgyz,

16
00:01:01,416 --> 00:01:03,780
so we'll add English captions as we go.

17
00:01:07,805 --> 00:01:13,164
The template gallery contains twelve
templates across six categories: university,

18
00:01:13,184 --> 00:01:17,215
school, IT projects, certificates,
reports and presentations.

19
00:01:17,639 --> 00:01:21,674
Every thumbnail is rendered live by
the same engine the editor uses,

20
00:01:21,694 --> 00:01:24,357
so what you see here is
exactly what you get.

21
00:01:24,777 --> 00:01:29,836
Search matches template names, descriptions
and tags. Let's search for certificates.

22
00:01:30,255 --> 00:01:34,830
Category chips narrow the list, and each
one shows how many templates it contains.

23
00:01:35,251 --> 00:01:39,860
There's also an orientation filter,
for portrait or landscape A4 sheets.

24
00:01:40,675 --> 00:01:43,702
Let's open the OkurmenKids
certificate in the editor.

25
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,063
The editor uses a three-column layout.

26
00:01:50,484 --> 00:01:55,627
On the left is the configuration panel, with
tabs for the document data, the template,

27
00:01:55,647 --> 00:01:56,468
and the style.

28
00:01:56,890 --> 00:02:01,512
In the center is a Fabric.js canvas,
drawn in exact A4 proportions,

29
00:02:01,532 --> 00:02:04,700
with zoom controls and
a fit-to-screen button.

30
00:02:05,123 --> 00:02:08,846
On the right are the properties of the
selected element, and the layers list.

31
00:02:09,268 --> 00:02:11,433
When I change the topic in the form,

32
00:02:11,453 --> 00:02:14,833
every text block that uses
that field updates instantly.

33
00:02:15,253 --> 00:02:18,664
Elements on the canvas can be
selected, dragged into place,

34
00:02:18,684 --> 00:02:20,467
and resized with their handles.

35
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:27,076
The properties panel gives precise control
over position, size, rotation and opacity.

36
00:02:28,236 --> 00:02:32,373
For text, I can change the font family,
the size, the weight and the color.

37
00:02:40,215 --> 00:02:45,356
The layers tab lists every element on the
page. Each layer can be reordered, hidden,

38
00:02:45,376 --> 00:02:45,970
or locked.

39
00:02:46,754 --> 00:02:52,538
The toolbar above the canvas adds new
elements: text, rectangles, ellipses, lines,

40
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:54,520
images and technology logos.

41
00:02:54,941 --> 00:02:58,415
Shapes have their own fill, stroke
and corner radius settings.

42
00:03:00,157 --> 00:03:02,423
Every action goes into the history,

43
00:03:02,443 --> 00:03:05,951
so undo and redo work with
the buttons or with Ctrl+Z.

44
00:03:08,001 --> 00:03:12,025
In the style tab, color presets
recolor the whole document at once,

45
00:03:12,045 --> 00:03:15,949
because templates reference theme
colors instead of fixed values.

46
00:03:16,370 --> 00:03:21,489
The background can be a solid color, a
gradient with an adjustable angle, or a photo.

47
00:03:21,909 --> 00:03:24,023
The OkurmenKids logo is built in,

48
00:03:24,043 --> 00:03:29,456
and a signature can be drawn right on the
screen with a mouse, a finger or a stylus.

49
00:03:33,756 --> 00:03:36,501
When a stamp or a
signature scan is uploaded,

50
00:03:36,521 --> 00:03:40,188
the paper background is removed
automatically, and the logo,

51
00:03:40,208 --> 00:03:44,490
stamp and signature can be saved to
a brand kit for every new project.

52
00:03:48,512 --> 00:03:54,180
When the design is ready, the download
dialog offers two formats: PDF for printing,

53
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,550
and PNG for sharing.

54
00:03:55,970 --> 00:04:04,349
The sheet can be A4 portrait or A4 landscape,
and there are three resolutions: 192,

55
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:05,968
300 and 384 DPI.

56
00:04:06,390 --> 00:04:09,485
The dialog shows the exact
output size in pixels,

57
00:04:09,505 --> 00:04:14,888
and because export uses the same renderer
as the canvas, the file matches the screen.

58
00:04:15,308 --> 00:04:19,141
The PDF is generated right
in the browser with jsPDF,

59
00:04:19,161 --> 00:04:21,904
which is loaded only when it's needed.

60
00:04:25,926 --> 00:04:29,475
There's no save button. The
editor autosaves every change,

61
00:04:29,495 --> 00:04:32,059
and the status in the top bar confirms it.

62
00:04:32,581 --> 00:04:37,615
All projects appear on the My Projects
page, sorted by when they were last edited,

63
00:04:37,635 --> 00:04:40,204
and each one can be duplicated or deleted.

64
00:04:40,626 --> 00:04:45,429
They're stored in the browser's local
storage, so they survive a page reload.

65
00:04:45,449 --> 00:04:50,566
Uploaded images are compressed and stored
once, and projects reference them by ID.

66
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:54,298
Clicking a project reopens it
exactly where you left off.

67
00:04:58,318 --> 00:05:03,520
Under the hood, Cover Studio is built
with React 19, TypeScript and Vite,

68
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:05,737
and styled with Tailwind CSS 4.

69
00:05:06,157 --> 00:05:11,703
State lives in Zustand stores, the
canvas is powered by Fabric.js 7,

70
00:05:11,723 --> 00:05:15,959
PDFs come from jsPDF, and
routing uses React Router.

71
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:20,326
Template definitions are
functions of the page size,

72
00:05:20,346 --> 00:05:24,522
so switching orientation rebuilds
the layout instead of stretching it.

73
00:05:24,942 --> 00:05:29,196
Text stores field placeholders, while
colors and fonts are theme tokens.

74
00:05:29,216 --> 00:05:33,471
That's why the form and the color
presets can update everything at once.

75
00:05:33,891 --> 00:05:38,634
The editor store holds the open document,
the selection, the undo history,

76
00:05:38,654 --> 00:05:43,525
zoom and preview mode. The project store
persists projects to local storage.

77
00:05:43,945 --> 00:05:47,082
A single Fabric renderer
draws the editor canvas,

78
00:05:47,102 --> 00:05:50,046
the gallery thumbnails
and the exported files.

79
00:05:50,066 --> 00:05:55,201
It only recreates objects whose content
changed, so the selection is never lost.

80
00:05:55,621 --> 00:06:01,321
Finally, two small utilities handle
PNG export and lazy-loaded PDF export.

81
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:09,229
Cover Studio is a static single-page
app, so deployment is simple.

82
00:06:09,649 --> 00:06:15,808
For Vercel, a rewrite rule in vercel.json
sends every route to index.html.

83
00:06:15,828 --> 00:06:20,484
For Netlify, the same rule
lives in the _redirects file.

84
00:06:20,906 --> 00:06:23,924
For hosts without rewrites,
such as GitHub Pages,

85
00:06:23,944 --> 00:06:28,574
a separate static build switches to
hash-based routing with relative paths.

86
00:06:29,843 --> 00:06:35,130
That's Cover Studio: a template-driven
document designer with a real canvas editor,

87
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:39,734
print-quality export and autosaved
projects, all running in the browser.

88
00:06:40,154 --> 00:06:42,619
Technically, it shows how one renderer,

89
00:06:42,639 --> 00:06:47,334
parametric templates and theme tokens
keep a complex editor consistent and

90
00:06:47,354 --> 00:06:48,098
predictable.

91
00:06:48,519 --> 00:06:54,525
The source code is on GitHub, at
github.com/Islam0122/cover-studio-okurmenkids.

92
00:06:54,545 --> 00:06:56,050
Thanks for watching!
